WEBVTT

00:52:58.600 --> 00:53:02.205
CA: You get a deduction
even if you're not paying taxes?

00:53:02.229 --> 00:53:06.237
DB: Right. You get it, basically,
an EITC-type credit. You get some refund.

00:53:06.261 --> 00:53:08.312
And so there are things I would do.

00:53:08.336 --> 00:53:10.737
I do think it's also important
to devolve power.

00:53:10.761 --> 00:53:15.122
I think devolving power out of Washington
and giving people actual local control

00:53:15.146 --> 00:53:18.061
is a way to really get them
active in their community.

00:53:18.085 --> 00:53:20.464
I was in, as I say, Nebraska yesterday.

00:53:20.488 --> 00:53:23.441
Nebraska's weird because
it's a state without too many people,

00:53:23.465 --> 00:53:25.100
but it's got 93 counties.

00:53:25.124 --> 00:53:27.913
Some of the counties only have
700 or 800 people in them,

00:53:27.937 --> 00:53:30.047
but they've still got
to have a school board,